================ PRODUCTION QUESTIONS =====================


27. TELL ME ABOUT A TIME WHEN YOU HANDLED A PRODUCTION ISSUE
------------------------------------------------------------

In my project, we faced a production issue where one of our
APIs was failing for some users, while it was working correctly
for most users.

First, I checked the application logs and identified the API
and the request where the issue was occurring.

Then I traced the request flow from the controller to the
service and database layers.

After analyzing the issue, I found that for some specific
records, an optional field was null or missing, and our code
was not handling that scenario properly.

Because of this, the API was throwing an exception.

I fixed the issue by adding proper null handling and validation
at the appropriate layer.

I also tested the API with both valid and missing-data scenarios.

After deploying the fix, I monitored the logs and API responses
to confirm that the issue was resolved.

I also reviewed similar code to prevent the same type of issue
from happening again.


28. WHY DID THE ISSUE HAPPEN IN PRODUCTION BUT NOT LOCALLY?
------------------------------------------------------------

The issue was data-dependent.

Our local test data did not contain the particular scenario
where the field was missing, so the issue was not reproduced
during normal testing.

In production, real-world data contained that scenario.


29. HOW DO YOU DEBUG A PRODUCTION ISSUE?
------------------------------------------------------------

First, I understand the issue and its impact.

Then I check the application logs, request and response details,
and identify the affected API or module.

After that, I trace the request flow through the controller,
service, database, or external service to find the root cause.

Once the issue is identified, I fix it carefully, test the
solution, deploy it, and monitor the application after
deployment.


30. TELL ME ABOUT A CRITICAL BUG YOU FIXED
------------------------------------------------------------

I faced an issue where an API was failing for certain users
because some records contained missing optional data.

I checked the logs, reproduced the scenario, traced the request
flow, and identified that the code was not handling the null
value correctly.

I added proper validation and null handling, tested different
scenarios, and deployed the fix.

After deployment, I monitored the API to make sure the issue
was completely resolved.


